## 3. Architecture (spec §8.1)

```
read-oasis/
  index.html, parent.html       child app / parent area (separate documents; child UI has no link into studio tools)
  assets/app.css                tokens (font px, line-height, column width, themes), 44px targets, reduced motion
  assets/icons/*.svg            original decorative icons (also inlined as a sprite in index.html)
  src/schema.mjs                schema v1, validateBook, checkDecodability, isPublishable, nextStatus
  src/progress-store.mjs        ProgressStore (storage-agnostic), migrations, ledger, backup, evidenceSummary, suggestLevelChange
  src/ui.mjs                    DOM helper, settings→CSS vars, narrator (audio asset or SpeechSynthesis), BreakTimer
  src/kid-app.mjs               Choose → Preview → Read/Listen → Think & tell → Activities → Quiz → Celebrate → Stop
  src/parent-dashboard.mjs      PIN gate, Evidence, Answers review, Baseline, Settings, Content studio, Data
  content/books/*.json          books (3 PUBLISHED originals + 1 CONTENT_REVIEW fixture that must stay hidden)
  content/images/*.svg          original illustrations with <title>/<desc>; story text never inside SVG
  content/phonics_lexicon.json  taught-word lists per pattern (C03 helper)
  content/index.json            GENERATED by tools/validate_content.py --index (PUBLISHED only, sha256 per file)
  tools/                        validate_content.py, gen_svgs.py, contrast_check.py, js_bracket_check.py
  test/                         schema.test.mjs, progress-store.test.mjs (node:test); test_validate_content.py (unittest)
  sw.js, manifest.webmanifest   offline shell
```

Why this stack: plain ES modules + static hosting is the simplest maintainable option that matches the
existing repo's deployment (drop files on GitHub Pages / any static server), needs no build, works offline,
and keeps every data write on-device. No framework, no analytics, no third-party requests.

**Data contract:** book schema fields are enforced in `validateBook`; progress is keyed
`books[book_id].revisions[revision]` so a new revision never overwrites old results (D06); every reward is a
ledger row keyed `child|book|revision|activity|question|cycle` (D01); attempts are append-only with
`first_attempt`, `support_used`, `unseen` flags so the dashboard can separate practice volume from evidence (L03).

## 4. Run

```
cd read-oasis
python3 -m http.server 8080          # any static server; ES modules need http(s), not file://
# child app:   http://localhost:8080/index.html
# parent area: http://localhost:8080/parent.html   (first visit sets a local PIN)
```

Add a book without touching reader code (L05): write `content/books/<id>.json`, put SVG/audio under
`content/images|audio/`, run `python3 tools/validate_content.py --index`. Only PUBLISHED + fully approved
books enter `index.json`. Bump `VERSION` in `sw.js` so offline caches refresh.

Regenerate illustrations: `python3 tools/gen_svgs.py`.

