## 6. Known limitations / honest gaps
- No Node on this host → JS unit tests are unexecuted; only a bracket/import sanity check ran (`tools/js_bracket_check.py`: 8/8 OK).
- Narration uses `SpeechSynthesis` when no verified audio file exists; voice quality varies by device. No audio assets are bundled yet.
- Parent PIN hashed with SHA-256 in secure contexts; on `file://` it degrades to plaintext and the UI says so. Not suitable for a shared/online service (spec §7, §10 "Online/public release").
- Break cue is a JS timer; it pauses when the tab is hidden and cannot measure real eye strain.
- Content studio approves drafts in-browser, but publishing to the child library is an explicit file step (`tools/validate_content.py --index`) so media checks and hashing always run. That is intentional, not a bug.
- Only three original books; the library must grow from the child's evidence, not a target count.

